WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:04.770
Euron Greyjoy: After Aegon and his dragons
burned our last king, Harren the Black, and

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:11.240
broke our armies, the defeated ironborn chose
my ancestor, Vickon Greyjoy, as Lord of the

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.580
Iron Islands, not king.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:19.380
The stories claimed that the Old Way died
with Harren the Black and his sons in Harrenhal.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:25.269
Our ships and axes were no match for Aegon's
dragons, so our ancestors bent their steel

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:31.800
into fishhooks and our kingdom into villages
and started telling the red tales around the

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:38.000
fire of how we used to be strong and how one
day we would be so again.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.160
Generations later, a young boy listened to
them.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:48.120
Dalton Greyjoy, the wild young heir to Pyke,
was rowing at five and reaving at ten in the

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.340
Basilisk Isles with his uncle.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:57.760
By fourteen, Dalton had sailed as far as Old
Ghis, fought in a dozen battles, and claimed

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.089
four salt wives.

00:00:59.089 --> 00:01:05.530
In his fifteenth year, he avenged his uncle's
death in battle, but he took a dozen wounds

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.930
and emerged from the fight drenched head to
heel in blood.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:15.190
From that day forth, men called him the Red
Kraken.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:22.000
During the Dance of Dragons, the Red Kraken
picked the side that was fighting the Lannisters

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.140
and fell upon the Westerlands while the Lannisters
were off at war.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:32.550
Casterly Rock itself proved too strong once
the lady of the castle barred its gates, but

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:38.950
the ironborn burned the Lannister fleet and
sacked Lannisport carrying off gold, grain,

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:44.200
and hundreds of women and girls, including
Lord Lannister's favorite mistress and all

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.009
his bastards.

00:01:46.009 --> 00:01:52.170
The Red Kraken now ruled the Sunset Sea as
his forbears had, and his longship once again

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.469
brought the Old Way to the coast of Westeros.

00:01:55.469 --> 00:01:59.520
But then the war ended, and the mainland armies
came home.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:06.659
The Iron Throne commanded the Red Kraken to
stop reaving, and when he didn't, a mistress

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.220
opened his throat as he slept.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:15.890
While his sons squabbled, the Lannisters sent
their soldiers to the Iron Islands.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:21.280
Thousands of men, women, and children were
put to the sword, and scores of villages and

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.800
hundreds of longships were put to the torch.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:30.490
The glorious return to the Old Way had lasted
two years.

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:36.560
Jaime: It should not be hard to recruit lords
into a war against an enemy known as "the

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.560
Mad King."

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.650
We can even understand the lords who chose
to honor their oaths and fight for him.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:48.200
But the krakens of House Greyjoy sat out Robert's
Rebellion on Pyke with their tentacles up

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.200
their arse.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.870
Euron: My father Quellon was old, and sitting
is what old people do best.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:55.620
Well, second best.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.930
He would have sat out the whole war if not
for my brother and me.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:06.380
We convinced him that nobody would fear the
walls of the sea if we curled up by our fires

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:09.620
while others feasted on the spoils of the
Mad King.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:16.380
So the old man creaked into his rusty armor
and set sail for the Reach only to be routed

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.600
by Tyrell longboats.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:24.760
When my father sadly fell in battle, my older
brother Balon beat a tactical retreat to his

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.400
own inheritance as the new Lord of the Iron
Islands.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:33.640
Jaime: I'd rather die in the Reach than live
on the Iron Islands.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.910
Euron: The roses are prettier to pluck.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:43.230
But my brother was getting old and felt that
longing to sit, and the Seastone Chair was

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.550
as good a place as any.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:51.680
Within a few years, he realized that sitting
is only fun if everyone else has to stand.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.190
He had the priest reforge...

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.230
No, that's not right.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:04:04.290
They picked up sticks on the beach, wove them
into a new ancient driftwood crown, and declared

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.710
Balon the King of the Iron Islands.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:13.290
Unfortunately for my brother, the other king
in Westeros, Robert Baratheon, was famously

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:19.259
bad at sharing, and his father-by-law and
Warden of the West, Tywin Lannister, had a

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:23.000
mighty fleet at Lannisport within striking
distance of the Iron Islands.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.690
Jaime: Yes, you were very clever.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:29.820
And how brave burning our ships at anchor
in the night.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:34.259
Euron: They would have burned the same in
daylight.

00:04:34.259 --> 00:04:35.840
Lions are lazy beasts.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.900
You didn't rouse them till long after I set
fire to your proud mane.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.760
I planned it all, you know?

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.400
My first torch took your father's flagship.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.620
If it makes you feel better, we didn't loot
it.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.259
Out of respect and time.

00:04:52.259 --> 00:05:00.240
Jaime: I don't think I ever saw Robert happier
than the day he heard about the Greyjoy Rebellion.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.270
He'd been king for a handful of years and
many handfuls of other things, and it was

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:09.919
clear to him and everyone else how ill-suited
he was to rule.

00:05:09.919 --> 00:05:12.810
But battle, he could do.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:18.740
Unfortunately, by the time we raised our army,
we seemed to be winning the war.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:24.919
Balon's eldest son, your nephew, died trying
to storm Seagard, and his men were thrown

00:05:24.919 --> 00:05:27.710
back into the arms of their Drowned God.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:32.930
If we wanted battle, we'd have to hurry north
before the ironborn put down their own rebellion.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.569
Euron: And we would have if I'd had my way.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:39.220
Rebelling was a stupid idea.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.600
Jaime: Never stopped your people before.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.509
Euron: Before Balon put those sticks on his
head, I told him that if he wanted to rule

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:52.080
the Iron Islands, all he had to do was give
King Robert a tour of them.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:58.310
Why waste our forces fighting a war we couldn't
win for a place our enemy wouldn't want?

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:03.599
With the Iron Fleet, we could reave not just
Westeros, but the rich lands beyond the Sunset

00:06:03.599 --> 00:06:04.599
Sea.

00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:08.250
But my brother was too attached to that Seastone
Chair.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:13.249
He commanded me to sail the Iron Fleet against
Robert's navy before he could ferry his army

00:06:13.249 --> 00:06:14.249
to Pyke.

00:06:14.249 --> 00:06:19.099
Jaime: A navy commanded by Robert's younger
brother Stannis, most known for sitting in

00:06:19.099 --> 00:06:22.310
a besieged castle eating dogs and horses.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:26.790
Remind me, how did you fare against a man
who'd never commanded ships in battle?

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.720
Euron: Nearly too well.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.449
Jaime: Stannis smashed your Iron Fleet at
Fair Isle.

00:06:32.449 --> 00:06:37.039
Euron: After I sailed it into a strait, where
our numbers and the size of our ships would

00:06:37.039 --> 00:06:38.210
work against us.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:43.169
It took some doing to convince my men to rush
into such an obvious trap.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:46.409
Stannis was not a subtle man.

00:06:46.409 --> 00:06:49.800
Jaime: You would rather claim treason than
defeat?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.270
Euron: Victory would have only delayed it.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:57.560
We couldn't hold off Robert's forces forever,
but we could waste enough ironborn that we

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.180
wouldn't even fill our own islands after the
war.

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:03.360
I made sure the Silence escaped.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.150
That was enough for me.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:09.830
That, and watching your army smash my brother's
castle soon afterwards.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.520
Jaime: Why didn't you just abandon him after
Fair Isle?

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.699
Why risk your precious life fighting for him
at Pyke?

00:07:16.699 --> 00:07:20.270
Euron: I wanted to kill the best knights in
Westeros.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:21.860
Jaime: You failed.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:23.439
Euron: So did you.

00:07:23.439 --> 00:07:26.379
I expected pursuit when I fled Pyke on the
Silence.

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:31.930
But I suppose you were too busy not punishing
my brother to not punish the man who burned

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.120
your father's fleet.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.050
Theon Greyjoy: Where the North has its honor
and the South its chivalry, the Iron Islands

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.050
has its strength.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:43.400
Yara Greyjoy: We call ourselves the "ironborn,"
and we are warriors feared throughout the

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:44.620
Seven Kingdoms.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:46.860
Theon: Or so we used to be.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:52.181
Unlike their mainland cousins, the First Men
of the Iron Islands never bowed to the Old

00:07:52.181 --> 00:07:53.181
Gods.

00:07:53.181 --> 00:07:58.439
Yara: Theirs was the Drowned God, who made
the ironborn to reave and sack and write their

00:07:58.439 --> 00:08:05.849
names in salt, steel, and song, that his enemy,
the Storm God, could not wash away.

00:08:05.849 --> 00:08:11.639
We raised our kings from our own ranks and
used beaten foes as thralls to work our mines

00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:12.960
and farm our land.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:16.360
Theon: Or as salt wives, if a woman was pretty
enough.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:23.879
Such was the Old Way, and while we followed
it, we held sway wherever the waves were heard.

00:08:23.879 --> 00:08:28.509
When Aegon came demanding fealty, King Harren
the Black ruled as far east as the Trident.

00:08:28.509 --> 00:08:35.121
Yara: Other kings, like the Starks, could
kneel, but Harren was ironborn, and the ironborn

00:08:35.121 --> 00:08:37.540
must be beaten.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:42.930
In Harrenhal, he had the mightiest castle
in Westeros, and the army to defend it.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:46.540
Theon: But Aegon did not intend a siege.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.960
He mounted his dragon and roasted Harren and
all his sons in their tower, and the old way

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.550
with them.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:56.680
Because of Harren's defiance, Aegon pushed
the Ironborn back to our islands and gave

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.410
the Riverlands to the Tullys.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:02.780
But he did allow the ironborn to choose who
would lead them.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:08.930
Yara: House Greyjoy had always been one of
the greatest houses of the Iron Islands.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:14.100
We trace their descent from the Age of Heroes
and the legendary Grey King, who took a mermaid

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:17.930
to wife and made war upon the Storm God for
a thousand years.

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:23.010
Theon: Blessed by the Drowned God, the Grey
King fought and slew Nagga, the great Sea

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:25.540
Dragon, and took her fire for his own.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:31.770
Yara: This history made our ancestor, Vickon
Greyjoy, the natural choice to lead the Ironborn

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:34.050
after Aegon's Conquest.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:39.050
For three hundred years, House Greyjoy ruled
the Ironborn.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:45.910
We style ourselves Lord of the Iron Islands,
King of Salt and Rock, Son of the Sea Wind,

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:47.920
Lord Reaper of Pyke.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.840
Theon: In truth, we were thralls.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:56.960
Our people still chanted "What is Dead May
Never Die," but the Old Way had died.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:03.150
Yara: Until the Targaryens followed their
dragons into the grave, and our lord father,

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:07.100
Balon Greyjoy, rose against the new king,
Robert Baratheon.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:12.340
Robb Stark: "Dark wings, dark words."

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:18.320
I was only a boy when the raven came to call
my father, Lord Eddard Stark, to another war.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:23.740
Balon Greyjoy had raised the Iron Islands
in revolt and burned the Lannister fleet at

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.240
anchor.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:29.090
King Robert Baratheon again needed his old
friend.

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:33.160
My mother, Catelyn, was not happy to lose
her lord husband to Robert again.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:37.600
Six years before, he had left her to avenge
his father and brother against the Mad King.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:44.190
But now he had sons and daughters of his own,
and, unspoken, another son who was not hers

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:46.760
from the last time he went to war.

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:49.850
My brother, Jon Snow.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:53.780
But she knew that in marrying my father, she
had married the North.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:57.420
We hold our honor and duty as dear as our
own gods.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:03.760
When the time came, my father marched south
to restore peace and order to the realm.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:08.370
My father always told me the Iron Islands
were a strange and dangerous place.

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:13.170
Its people, the ironborn, keep neither the
Old Gods of the Forest nor The Seven and despise

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:15.030
all honest toil.

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:20.070
Their ancestors ravaged the western shores,
and putting it to the torch, and their songs

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:25.540
still ring through the halls of the ironborn
while everywhere else they're whispered to

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:28.190
wayward children at bedtime.

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:32.900
Perhaps Lord Balon thought Westeros had not
healed from the war against the Mad King and

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:39.470
was as fragmented and suspicious as the ancient
kingdoms his forbears had terrorized.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:44.860
Robert's navy corrected him at Fair Isle when
they smashed the proud Iron Fleet.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:50.650
Robert and my father corrected him at Pyke
when they pulled down his towers and breached

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:52.830
his walls.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:59.490
My father never liked to speak of his battles,
but, from other men, I learned what transpired.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:03.970
Thoros of Myr was first through the breach
with his flaming sword.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:08.410
Not far behind him was Jorah Mormont of Bear
Island, my father's bannerman who earned the

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:14.150
knighthood he would later shame, and lords
from every corner of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:18.440
All day through every passage of the castle,
they fought side by side.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:23.610
My father with our ancestral sword Ice and
King Robert with his warhammer against a horde

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:26.440
of ax-wielding ironborn.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:31.440
In the end, Lord Balon bent the knee.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:37.230
King Robert generously allowed Lord Balon
to retain his title and castle.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.830
The price of peace was custom.

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:45.060
The only son of Balon's to survive his foolish
rebellion would be taken as a hostage against

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:47.500
future treasons.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:54.510
My father even volunteered to foster the boy
himself, I suspect to make Theon Greyjoy a

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:59.560
different man than his father, who would bring
honor and duty to the Iron Islands when he

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:02.170
returned as heir.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:06.840
So my mother's silent fear came true, and
my father returned with another child.

